📊 Data Visualization & Insight Strategy

Our project focuses on transforming complex wind turbine sensor data into clear, actionable visual insights for operators and decision-makers. Rather than only building predictive models, we prioritized how anomalies and trends are presented, ensuring that potential issues can be quickly understood and acted upon.

🎯 Core Approach

We designed an interactive and intuitive visualization framework that:

Highlights early warning signals in turbine performance
Compares normal vs. anomalous behavior across time and turbines
Enables fleet-level monitoring with drill-down capabilities

Our goal was to bridge the gap between raw time-series data and real-world operational decisions.

🔍 Key Visualization Features
1. Time-Series Anomaly Tracking

We display multi-sensor data (e.g., temperature, vibration, pressure) through layered time-series plots that:

Show baseline vs. deviation patterns
Highlight pre-failure trends leading up to labeled events
Allow users to zoom into specific time windows for detailed inspection

These views help answer: How early can we visually detect abnormal behavior?

2. Comparative Turbine Views

To support cross-turbine and cross-farm analysis, we implemented:

Side-by-side comparisons of turbines under similar conditions
Aggregated views to distinguish normal operating ranges vs. outliers
Visual thresholds to indicate risk levels

This enables users to quickly identify whether an issue is isolated or systemic.

3. Thermal & Electrical Heatmaps

We use heatmaps to represent temperature and electrical indicators across time:

Color gradients emphasize subtle shifts and spikes
Patterns reveal gradual overheating or irregularities
Useful for spotting anomalies that may not be obvious in raw plots
4. Anomaly Scoring & Alerts

We visualize anomaly detection outputs (e.g., reconstruction error, statistical thresholds) through:

Score timelines showing severity over time
Clearly marked alert zones for operator attention
Optional explainability overlays to show contributing sensors

This helps reduce false alarms while ensuring early detection of critical issues.

5. Fleet-Level Dashboard

Our dashboard provides a high-level overview of turbine health:

Summary metrics (e.g., anomaly frequency, risk scores)
Farm-level comparisons (onshore vs. offshore)
Drill-down capability from fleet → turbine → sensor level

This allows decision-makers to monitor overall reliability at scale.

💡 Design Principles
Clarity over complexity: Visuals are designed for fast interpretation, not just technical depth
Actionable insights: Every chart answers a practical operational question
Scalability: The system can extend from a single turbine to an entire wind farm
Explainability: Users can understand why a signal is flagged, not just that it is
🚀 Impact

By focusing on visualization and interpretability, our approach:

Enables earlier and more confident fault detection
Reduces unnecessary maintenance through clearer insights
Improves communication between data scientists and turbine operators
